# .yummi.conf.example — template for Yummi's local configuration.
#
# You normally do NOT write this file by hand: run `make conf` for an
# interactive setup that persists your choices to a gitignored `.yummi.conf`
# (masked entry for any API key). It's deliberately short — container engine
# and UI language are auto-detected, and picking a model is ONE question
# (local: just a model name, cloud: just an API key). This example documents
# every field that file CAN hold, including the ones `make conf`'s simple
# path never asks about, so you can see the full set at a glance — or copy
# it to `.yummi.conf` and edit directly if you prefer.
#
#   cp .yummi.conf.example .yummi.conf
#
# The real `.yummi.conf` is gitignored and never committed. This file is
# make-syntax (KEY=value, `#` comments) because the root Makefile `-include`s
# it, so every `make build`/`make start`/etc. picks these up automatically.

# ── Container engine ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docker | podman. `make conf` auto-detects this (OrbStack/Docker Desktop via
# the active `docker context`, else Podman, else Linux native) and only asks
# if nothing could be detected. On macOS, OrbStack (used as the docker
# engine) is the recommended, no-workarounds option — see docs/installation.md.
CONTAINER_ENGINE=docker

# ── Network mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# secure          — the default; yummi_internal is `internal: true`, so the
#                   sandbox's only path out is through the gateway. Always
#                   paired with CONTAINER_ENGINE=docker by `make conf`.
# insecure-bridge — compatibility workaround that restores ordinary bridge
#                   egress; weakens the fail-closed topology. What `make conf`
#                   pairs with podman (podman's own networking needs it) or
#                   Docker Desktop if picked manually. Only use this with
#                   docker if you understand the trade-off (docs/installation.md).
YUMMI_NETWORK_MODE=secure

# ── UI display language (build-time) ────────────────────────────────────────
# en | tr. Baked into the UI at build time; there is no runtime switch.
# `make conf` suggests tr when your shell's $LANG looks Turkish, en otherwise
# — either way it's one keypress (or Enter) to confirm, never silently forced.
YUMMI_LANG=en

# ── Agentic engine ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# graph — tag-protocol state machine. eino — native tool-calling ReAct loop,
# with full cataloged-tool and terminal-session parity with graph as of
# 2026-10-07. `make conf` always sets eino now, for both the local and cloud
# model paths — there's no longer a meaningful reason to pick graph over it
# on a fresh setup. Runtime-only either way: change it without rebuilding.
YUMMI_AGENT_BACKEND=eino

# ── Model: pick ONE of the three shapes below ───────────────────────────────
# `make conf`'s model question is exactly these three choices. Local asks
# only a model name; Cloud/Custom asks only (plus a model name with a sane
# default) an API key — everything else in this section is filled in for you.

# 1) Local (Ollama) — just a model tag. A 20B-class model (the Ollama default
#    below) is fine for trying the chat/UI flow, but is NOT reliable for
#    autonomous multi-step tasks (confirmed: it can lose track of the target,
#    invent tool syntax, or fabricate an entire fake exploit run with zero
#    real tool calls). For real autonomous use this needs to be 120B+ — e.g.
#    gpt-oss:120b, which `make conf` offers as its own default. See
#    orchestrator/internal/conductor/tier.go's DefaultTierRegistry doc
#    comment for the full writeup.
YUMMI_OLLAMA_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b
# Optional: override the context window for a custom model tag (default: the
# resolved tier's own value). Not asked by `make conf`'s simple path — hand-edit
# if you need it.
#YUMMI_OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=32768

# 2) Cloud (OpenRouter/OpenAI) — just an API key. `make conf`'s Cloud choice
#    fills in the base URL/provider below for you and defaults the model name
#    to deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3.1 (confirmed working end to end against a
#    real multi-stage exploit chain) unless you type a different one.
#YUMMI_EINO_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#YUMMI_EINO_MODEL_NAME=deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3.1
#YUMMI_EINO_MODEL_API_KEY=
#YUMMI_EINO_PROVIDER=openrouter

# 3) Custom endpoint (LM Studio, vLLM, llama.cpp, a different OpenAI-compatible
#    server) — `make conf`'s third model choice; asks base URL, model name,
#    and an optional API key.
#YUMMI_EINO_MODEL_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1
#YUMMI_EINO_MODEL_NAME=openai/gpt-oss-20b
#YUMMI_EINO_MODEL_API_KEY=
#YUMMI_EINO_PROVIDER=openai

# ── Optional: "brain" frontier-model runner (docs: brain/README.md) ─────────
# `make conf` asks this once, at the end, defaulting to skip. If you already
# configured an OpenRouter key above, it offers to reuse it here with zero
# extra typing; otherwise it's the same one-key, one-model-name shape as the
# Cloud model choice above.
#YUMMI_BRAIN_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#YUMMI_BRAIN_MODEL_NAME=deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3.1
#YUMMI_BRAIN_MODEL_API_KEY=      # your key — stored only in the gitignored .yummi.conf
